    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d178">

                <pb facs="0307" n="273" sameAs="frus:frus1948v02/pg273"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Council/5–2448: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Caffery</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-05-24T18:00:00+01:00">May 24, 1948—6 p.
                            m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2755. In further explanation of why Bidault
                    gave me the two notes (mytel 2720 and 2724 May
                        21<anchor n="1" xml:id="d178-f1"/>), Chauvel gave me to understand that Bidault is in a panic over the attitude of the non-Communist
                    French press during the past two weeks in regard to the London conversations and
                    is especially concerned over the attitude of the Socialists whom he expected to
                    be friendly to his position. (He was not referring to very recent articles
                    obviously inspired by the Quai d’Orsay. I have <pb facs="0308" n="274"
                        xml:id="pg274"/> referred to these articles and let the French Government
                    know in plain terms what I think of them.)</p>
                <p>In other words Bidault now fears that he
                    has gone too far to meet us at London and is trying to find a way to crawl
                    out.</p>
                <p>Sent Department 2755; repeated London 426 and Berlin 241.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d178-f1" n="1" xml:id="d178-f1-content">
                <p>Neither the notes nor the telegrams under reference here are printed, but see
                    telegram 2214, May 21, from London, <ref target="#pg266">p. 266</ref>, and
                    footnotes 2 and 3 thereto.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
